  "assumptions": [
    "Idealised model: small-angle period T = 2π√(L/g), g = 9.81 m/s², fixed 10° swing; real swings at 10° are about 0.2% slower.",
    "Light, unstretchable string and point-like bob; no air resistance or friction, so the swing never dies down.",
    "The swing angle is computed from absolute time, so changing the length jumps the swing to the matching point of the new motion at the current time, and the motion may jump when the 60 s timeline loops."
  ],
  "program": {
    "source": "export function evaluate({ inputs, time }) {\n  const L = inputs.length;\n  const T = 2 * Math.PI * Math.sqrt(L / 9.81);\n  const a0 = 10 * Math.PI / 180;\n  const th = a0 * Math.cos(2 * Math.PI * time / T);\n  return {\n    nodes: {\n      pivot: { quaternion: [0, 0, Math.sin(th / 2), Math.cos(th / 2)] },\n      stringN: { position: [0, -L / 2, 0], scale: [1, L, 1] },\n      bobN: { position: [0, -L, 0] }\n    },\n    readouts: { period: T, len: L, angle: th * 180 / Math.PI }\n  };\n}\n"
  }
